    "description": "A spreadsheet calculation engine has an ExpressionParser, a FormulaCompiler, and a FormulaEvaluator. Users can define arithmetic, comparison, percentage, logical, assignment, ternary, indexing, and postfix operators, while plug-ins may register new operator tokens. Every operator has a declared precedence and association, and formulas must accept forms such as -value, a + b * c, x = y, flag ? yes : no, and value%. The current implementation contains many nearly identical expression functions, one for each precedence band, and adding an operator often requires changes in several branches. The language team wants all precedence and association information centralized in an operator registry, while still allowing each operator to have its own semantic handler in FormulaCompiler. Diagnostics must identify the operator and operand that failed, and parsing must remain deterministic and forward-only. The decision concerns expression parsing only; statement parsing is limited to assignment wrappers.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose how to encode precedence, association, and operand handling for a growing set of prefix, infix, postfix, and mixfix expression operators.",
    "notes": "Pratt-parser fits because precedence and association live in one operator registry with per-operator handlers; recursive-descent-parser is the per-precedence-band alternative, normalized AST and nested-scope table support the output."
  },
